course: dictionary
lesson: 15171
title: Words from holy writings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one subject, like church or religion. Scriptural is one of them. It comes from scripture, a word for holy writings. Context helps you find its meaning: «The vicar read a scriptural passage about kindness.» A passage from holy writing is being read, so scriptural must mean connected with those writings.
explain: Look for the ending -al. It often turns a noun into an adjective, so scripture becomes scriptural, like nature becomes natural. «Our RE lesson studied the scriptural teaching on forgiveness.» Teaching taken from holy writings is what makes it scriptural.
explain: Scriptural is not only about Christianity. Other faiths have their own scriptures, such as the Qur'an, the Torah and the Vedas. «The class compared the scriptural stories of three faiths.» Each faith's holy writings can be called scriptural.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The vicar read a passage from holy writings about kindness» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If you are not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: Scriptural means based on or connected with holy writings, especially the Bible.
fact: Scripture is a word for holy writings, and scriptural is the adjective made from it.
fact: «A scriptural reading» is a passage from holy writings, often read aloud in church.
fact: Other faiths have scriptures too: the Qur'an (Islam), the Torah (Judaism) and the Vedas (Hinduism).
fact: «Scriptural basis» means a reason or support for something that comes from holy writings.
exercise: «The vicar gave a scriptural reading about the Good Samaritan.» What does scriptural mean here? | About a sports match | *Connected with holy writings | Very loud and clear | A sad old song
exercise: Scriptural is built from a shorter word. Which word is it? | *scripture | scary | sculpture | scrub
exercise: Which faith's holy writings is the Torah? | Football | Hinduism | *Judaism
test: «Our class studied the scriptural teaching on sharing.» What does scriptural mean? | *Based on holy writings | About school dinners | Written in pencil
test: The Vedas are holy writings of which faith? | Gardening | *Hinduism | Judaism
exam: Which phrase names a passage read from holy writings? | scriptural fog | scriptural lunch | *scriptural reading
